     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Dear all,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"gmail_default\">My name is Irene and I am a PhD student who is planning, with my colleagues in Ecuador, <span><span>a distance sampling survey \r\nof spider monkeys in a tropical forest. We aim to measure \r\nperpendicular distances to the monkeys using laser range finders, but we\r\n are unsure about which range finder model should we buy. Distances \r\nare likely to be between 10-50 m.  D</span></span>oes anyone have been estimating distances in similar conditions and have a preferred range finder model?  All recommendations/suggestions are more than welcome.</div><div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"gmail_default\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"gmail_default\">Also, <span><span>another researcher, Frazer Sinclair, asked a similar question some days ago. Would you be able to share your answers to his question (if any)?</span></span> <br></div><div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"gmail_default\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\" class=\"gmail_default\">Thank you in advance!</div><div></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><span><span><span><span><div><br></div><div>Best regards,</div></span></span> <br></span></span></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><span><span>Irene</span></span></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><span><span><br></span></span>\r\n\r\n</div><div><div dir=\"ltr\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(0,255,0)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Irene Duch-Latorre</span><br>\r\n</span></span></span></font></div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n</span></span></font><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(0,255,0)\"></span>PhD Student, Department of Anthropology, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">UW-Madison</span></span> <br> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a href=\"https://strierlab.anthropology.wisc.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://strierlab.anthropology.wisc.edu/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474013963000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1M7lAHgzGTRAsfgbrgD_Bs\">Strier Lab – Primate Behavioral Ecology and Conservation</a></span><br></span></span></font> <font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><a href=\"https://www.proyectowashu.org/\" title=\"https://www.proyectowashu.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.proyectowashu.org/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792474013963000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3qC0A4bhBwUMA7w_CXxZfk\"><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Proyecto Washu</span></span></a></span></font></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
